  "description": "IGUJIG crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I 41/a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C76 H92 Gd4 N16 O16,4(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1I (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1K (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.837-3.837 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 109.97-113.69°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C80H104Gd4N16O20.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
